# Start first: dotnet run --project 17-CellBased\Cell.Launcher   (router :5117 + cells c1, c2, c3)
# The customers only talk to the router; the response says which cell served it (X-Cell header).
@router = http://localhost:5117
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@david = 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555

### Who is where: alice and david in c1, bob and emma in c2, carla in c3
GET {{router}}/platform/placement

### State of the cells: capacity, customers, version, health
GET {{router}}/platform/cells

### Bob's account (X-Cell: c2)
GET {{router}}/customers/bob/accounts

### Transfer Alice → David: same cell, local transaction ("crossCell": false)
POST {{router}}/customers/alice/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "targetCustomer": "david", "target": "{{david}}", "amount": 50 }

### Transfer Alice → Bob: two cells, local debit then credit through the router ("crossCell": true)
POST {{router}}/customers/alice/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "targetCustomer": "bob", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 100 }

### ─── Blast radius: cell c2 goes down (or stop its process) ───
PUT http://localhost:5232/admin/outage
Content-Type: application/json

{ "down": true }

### Bob and Emma: 503. Alice, Carla and David: 200.
GET {{router}}/customers/bob/accounts

###
GET {{router}}/customers/alice/accounts

### A transfer to Bob is cancelled, and Alice's debit compensated
POST {{router}}/customers/alice/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "targetCustomer": "bob", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 100 }

###
PUT http://localhost:5232/admin/outage
Content-Type: application/json

{ "down": false }

### ─── Deployment in waves ───
### The 1.1 contains a bug: the probe of the canary cell (c1) detects it, rollback, c2 and c3 received nothing
POST {{router}}/platform/deployments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": "1.1" }

### The 1.2 fixes it: c1 first, then c2 and c3
POST {{router}}/platform/deployments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": "1.2" }

### ─── Capacity: cells are added, not enlarged ───
### New customers: each one goes to the least loaded cell (3 places per cell, 9 in all)
POST {{router}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "farid", "name": "Farid", "initialDeposit": 20 }

### Provision the cell c4 (dotnet run --project 17-CellBased\Cell.Launcher -- c4), then register it
POST {{router}}/platform/cells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "c4", "url": "http://localhost:5234", "capacity": 3 }

### Move Carla to c4 (rebalancing): her data and her routing follow
POST {{router}}/platform/customers/carla/migrate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "c4" }

### Close c1 to new customers (before emptying it, for example)
POST {{router}}/platform/cells/c1/close
